[list]
[*]Stands now dress for the work types added by FrozenSnowFox's Complex Jobs. That mod splits vanilla's work into finer pieces and moves the tasks across: surgery leaves Doctor for Surgeon, feeding and rescuing patients leave it for Nurse, butchering leaves Cooking for Butcher, taming and training leave Handling for Train, drug synthesis leaves Crafting for Drugs, and stonecutting, smelting, machining, fabrication and refining each get a work type of their own. Shift Change was matching only the vanilla names, so a stand served whatever stayed behind and ignored everything that moved.
[*]That is why it read as unreliable rather than broken. A hospital stand still dressed a doctor to tend a patient, then sat there when the same colonist went to operate. A kitchen stand caught cooking and not butchering. A barn stand caught milking and shearing, which are not what most barn work is.
[*]What each room picks up: hospital adds Nurse and Surgeon, laboratory adds Drugs, kitchen adds Butcher, workshop adds Stone Cut, Smelt, Machining, Fabricate, Refine and Production, barn adds Train, Tame and slaughter.
[*]Nothing changes if you do not run Complex Jobs. A stand serves the same vanilla work types it served in 1.3.2, and a stand whose work list you set by hand keeps exactly the list you gave it. Only stands left on automatic pick up the additions.
[*]Tame and slaughter exist as separate work types only if you turn them on in Complex Jobs' own settings, which needs XML Extensions. A stand covers them when they are there and passes over them when they are not.
[/list]
